; Tutorial_3_Convert_PDFs_to_Markdown.inix -- a spoken walk through BatCon, written for buildTutorials (the format is
; described at the top of Tutorial_0_Overview.inix in the Homer kit's Templates).

[about]
Title=3 - Convert PDFs to Markdown
Intro=A folder of PDF files, each made a Markdown file you can read line by line.
Setup=BatCon is open, and a folder holds a few PDF files.
Homework=Convert a folder of your own PDFs.

[step]
Say=In Source files, type the folder and a pattern, here C colon backslash Reports backslash star dot P D F.
Key=Alt+S
Hear=Source files: edit

[step]
Say=Tab away, and BatCon finds the files and lists what they convert to.
Key=Tab
Hear=Browse source... button

[step]
Say=Alt plus T, Tango, for Target format, and Markdown is already first.
Key=Alt+T
Hear=Target format: list box
Hear=Markdown (md)

[step]
Say=Enter starts the batch. BatCon says how many files, then names each as it goes.
Key=Enter
Hear=Converting 3 files to md
Hear=2 of 3: Budget.pdf

[step]
Say=At the end, a window lists each file. Scanned pages are read with Tesseract, when it is installed.
Hear=3 files converted, 0 skipped, 0 failed.

[step]
Say=What this walk taught: a pattern in Source files, Markdown in Target format, and Enter.
